      {
        "claim_id": "policy-transmission-countercase",
        "claim_text": "The strongest countercase to treating the announcement as a verdict on borrowing costs is that instructions are not transactions. These documents supply no observed effective funding rates or matched bank deposit and loan rates, so they cannot establish how much of the decision reached bank customers. An account of policy transmission needs those observations as well as the announced settings.",
